    "millsfield:images_texts": [
      "Wine List\nEmirates\nDE",
      "CRU\nTÊT\nCHATEAU-FUISSE\nAlouilly-Fuisse\nSMOKING LOON\n2007 CALIFORNIA\nDINOT CRICKE\nBusiness Class\nWhite Wine\nChâteau Fuissé,\nTête de Cru, Pouilly Fuissé\n2005\nThe cream of the crop. Château Fuissé\nproduced textbook wines in the great\n2005 vintage. A truly versatile food\nwine; its minerality underlines the salty\nsea character of all fish types and\ncrustaceans. It's ripe fruitiness, crisp\nacidity and length, allow a marriage with\nspiced foods, as well as white meat.\nSmoking Loon\nPinot Grigio, California\n2007\nThe 2007 Smoking Loon Pinot Grigio\nbeckons with aromas of grapefruit and\nfresh sliced oranges, flavours of\nnectarines, mandarin oranges, limestone\nand a finish of minerals and lemongrass.\nAn easy and refreshing wine brimming\nwith sunshine coast verve.\nChitrun raint Bages\nNorfolk Rise\nSHIRAZ. 2005\nBusiness Class\nRed Wine\nChâteau Croizet Bages\nGrand Cru, Pauillac\n1996\nThe excellent 1996 was a catalyst for a\nreturn to form for Croizet Bages and this\nis amply shown as this wine unfurls in\nyour glass. Its high perfume is overlain\nwith dense aromas of ripe red fruit. On\nthe palate, a melting amalgam of cassis,\nspice and truffiles, with a long lingering\nfinish.\nNorfolk Rise Shiraz\nSouth Australia\n2005\nThe Limestone Coast is the source for\nthis juicy offering. Spotlessly clean and\npure blackberry and dark plum fruit\nooze forth. Medium-bodied with a\nfreshness that gives it some animation.\nClassic deep but easy drinking Shiraz."
    ],
